@@ -100,19 +100,31 @@ Each pet is recorded against exactly one owner, with a name, a birth date, and a
 
 ### Visits
 
-<a id="req-vis-001"></a><a id="req-vis-002"></a>
+<a id="req-vis-001"></a><a id="req-vis-002"></a><a id="req-vis-003"></a>
 
 A visit is booked against a particular pet and carries the date it is for and a short description of what it is for `[REQ-VIS-001]`. When booking, the pet's earlier visits are shown alongside, so whoever is booking can see what has already been done `[REQ-VIS-002]`.
 
+A booked visit can be corrected afterwards. Staff open the visit, see its stored date and description, and submit a replacement pair. The correction is held to the same rules as booking, and it changes that one visit rather than adding another to the pet `[REQ-VIS-003]`. Cancelling a booked visit stays out of scope (NG-5), as does deleting one (NG-4). Correction is reachable only by a reader who already knows the visit's address. This requirement adds no link to the correction form from the owner's record; a follow-up request may add one.
+
 **Done when:**
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a pet, when a description and a date later than today are supplied, then the visit is recorded and the booking is confirmed.
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a blank description, when the visit is submitted, then the booking is refused and the description is named.
 - `[REQ-VIS-001]` given a date of today or earlier, when the visit is submitted, then the booking is refused and the date is named.
 - `[REQ-VIS-002]` given a pet with earlier visits, when a new visit is being booked, then those earlier visits are shown with their dates and descriptions.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a booked visit, when it is opened for correction, then the same form as booking is shown, carrying that visit's stored date and description.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a booked visit, when a description and a date later than today are submitted, then that visit carries the new pair and the owner's record is shown.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a pet holding one visit, when that visit is corrected, then the pet still holds exactly one visit.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a blank description, when the correction is submitted, then the correction is refused and the description is named.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given a date of today or earlier, when the correction is submitted, then the correction is refused and the date is named.
+- `[REQ-VIS-003]` given an owner's record, when it is opened, then it offers no way to reach the correction form.
 
 **Edge cases:**
 1. Booking a visit for a pet that does not belong to the named owner is refused.
 2. The date offered by default is the earliest date that would be accepted.
+3. Correcting a visit that does not exist is refused rather than recording a new one.
+4. A refused correction leaves the stored visit as it was, and redisplays the submitted values for another attempt.
+
+**ADR:** [ADR: Correcting a Booked Visit Narrows NG-5](adr/2026-08-08-non-goal-visit-correction.md)
 
